CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default-init leaves storage: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ value-init zero then DMI: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [expr.new]/17: `::new(p) int` default-initializes (storage kept),
`::new(p) podt()` value-initializes (zero, then the default member
initializer b = 5).  Header-free; runtime-verified g++ 13 / clang++ 18
with a placement-new definition returning its pointer.  (The first
assertion relies on CBMC keeping the prior value under
default-initialization, which is one valid indeterminate value.)
